<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$5.00/cubic metre or C$0.79/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$204.00/cubic metre, or C$32.43/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$199.00/cubic metre, or C$31.64/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$180.00/cubic metre, or C$28.62/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$188.00/cubic metre, or C$29.89/barrel</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
